<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11, 2001 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:359678b7a879278cfecfc96046dcec23543ff3886a63d7ab50c9fd0b79689ae3</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918--22a07e00351f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg, via the so-called Hamburg cell, whose members played key roles in the plot. A look back at a day that shook up Germany’s approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc39b2cf321313444f7feb2bd82943d72c9b3e772a731683b7ec3fdf5e0c82fb</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran tightens social control with crackdown on cafes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1597d1ce37b3f2ac5650671dfde5e8e8983073eaa4be677bbc000e8dc3c2fc4b</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988--56f8af8e2572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities are keeping a close eye on cafes, fearing they could play a role in fostering anti-government sentiment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's constitutional reform: What does it mean — especially for Abiy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fe16e17b8a5ada0ff4e617247bc3d1a9aaf028980db1af828d3727019da22bd</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262--7aa1de37183a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed stands to benefit from a planned constitutional reform in the country. A new presidential system would reshape political power — and could give him a more powerful mandate in office.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Syria arms depot explosion kills at least 14</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5402983747137e5a257e32575c8060a2c6aeae6f6ae159cd7782992f2e79a403</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314--22d7b8669d08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion struck near the Syrian city of Sarmada in Idlib province in the northwest. The Defense Ministry said the weapons and remnants from the war were being stored temporarily at the site before being relocated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:292923f208538a6091dd13a4d21d9ebc23ba0d7089cc0b0886b2bc98d979412c</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: How  the 'house of sisters' threat split society</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56659e2e406b46a129225919221fdef238516c7cb332be89844076c8fb1e84c0</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163--b9de2b546f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rumor has it that the 'house of sisters' is where kidnapped women from other Syrian sects are forced to convert to Islam. Nobody knows if it really exists, but it's being used to create communal tensions anyway.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63bbf3f442c98d4798bbfc631381f5583ad78932aa31b3e63004651db18f9651</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c0c754c2ba514f749d2275c52dda4ca25be102a3de9bb3d2ff0c6b9fe79a2a8</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386--b343555e2833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s President Vladimir Putin has dismissed rumors about military mobilization. But many Russians, including many DW users, say they are preparing for the possibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dallas Republican convention: How Trump looms over midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d143b8e255a62b270b27ce0d32b1b24251132254b81e193c990e439f8f10e62</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dallas-republican-convention-how-trump-looms-over-midterms/a-79189744--12ee322d24e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dallas-republican-convention-how-trump-looms-over-midterms/a-79189744?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump is not on the ballot in the midterm elections — but the first Republican midterm convention is putting him center stage. It's a strategy that could prove risky for the party.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8f6a8ae3d28f4e865b53016fc306c84641924cc6971a8d66debabf002439f67</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Mao Zedong's legacy still shapes China 50 years on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30f481d6e5245a94db4eec53cbf85ac622ed1d36e5e2b7297d7e87aaff9821f3</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-mao-zedong-s-legacy-still-shapes-china-50-years-on/a-79189751--83b4fb70b8d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-mao-zedong-s-legacy-still-shapes-china-50-years-on/a-79189751?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has transformed since Mao Zedong's death 50 years ago. But his legacy endures — from Xi Jinping's rule to a new wave of Mao nostalgia among young Chinese.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
